window.CASE = {"id":"d-tomb","meta":{"title":"The Seventh Chamber","titleHtml":"The Seventh <i>Chamber</i>","eyebrow":"Valley of the Kings, Upper Egypt · December 1923","cover":"For three thousand years nobody had looked behind the sealed doorway. The morning the press arrived to see it, the expedition's leader was lying dead inside.","aerial":"img/d-tomb/aerial.jpg","aerialCaption":"The Vane Expedition's camp below the hillside, December 1923. For the look of it only: go by the plan below."},"imgdir":"img/d-tomb/","stage1":{"officer":"Inspector Fawzi","suspectsTitle":"The camp","suspectsIntro":"Four people in the camp had reason to quarrel with Sir Roderick.","briefing":"\n    <p class=\"dateline\">LUXOR POLICE · THURSDAY 13th DECEMBER 1923 · 9.00 A.M.</p>\n    <h2>The death of Sir Roderick Vane</h2>\n    <img class=\"victim\" src=\"img/d-tomb/victim.jpg\" alt=\"Sir Roderick Vane\">\n    <p>At a quarter past six this morning <b>Sir Roderick Vane</b>, 62, leader of the Vane Expedition, was found dead inside the <b>Seventh Chamber</b> of Tomb 71, the tomb of the treasurer Djehuty-ankh, in the Valley of the Kings. He had been struck once on the back of the head.</p>\n    <p>Yesterday afternoon his workmen broke a small hole through the sealed doorway of the Seventh Chamber, the first look inside for three thousand years. The newspapermen were to see it at ten this morning. Instead Sir Roderick was lying at the back of it, although the tomb gate was locked all night and no grown man could squeeze through that hole.</p>\n    <p>Cairo and London are already talking about a curse. I do not believe in curses. I believe in sand, lamps and people.</p>\n    <figure class=\"photo tilt\"><img src=\"img/d-tomb/breach.jpg\" alt=\"The sealed doorway with the breach\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Doorway VII, with yesterday's breach at the top. Photographed by Miss Marsh at 4 p.m.</figcaption></figure>\n    <p>The case comes in <b>three stages</b>, and each question is revealed only when you reach it. <b>Stage I:</b> How did Sir Roderick get into the Seventh Chamber?</p>\n    <p class=\"sig\">— Ahmed Fawzi Effendi, Inspector, Luxor Police</p>","suspects":[{"id":"coyle","name":"Dr Leonard Coyle","age":46,"height":"5 ft 11 in","role":"Epigrapher, deputy leader","bio":"Reads hieroglyphs and the old running hand, hieratic, and makes plaster casts of statues and inscriptions for the museums at home. Twelve seasons at Sir Roderick's side. Writes everything in green ink.","interest":"Says he spent the whole night at his desk writing up the Seventh Chamber's docket for the press, and that the guard saw him there."},{"id":"evelyn","name":"Miss Evelyn Marsh","age":29,"height":"5 ft 5 in","role":"Expedition photographer","bio":"One of very few women working in the Valley. She photographs every stage of the dig and develops her own plates at night in the darkroom tent.","interest":"Yesterday Sir Roderick caught her posting prints of the breach to the <i>Daily Courier</i>, breaking his exclusive contract with another paper. He swore she would never work in Egypt again."},{"id":"hanafi","name":"Dr Yusuf Hanafi","age":41,"height":"5 ft 10 in","role":"Inspector of Antiquities, Upper Egypt","bio":"Trained in Cairo and Berlin, and reads the old inscriptions as well as anyone in the Valley. He is posted to the camp to see that the new rule is kept: what is found in Egypt stays in Egypt.","interest":"Holds the Antiquities Service's key to the tomb gate. Quarrelled openly with Sir Roderick, who wanted half the finds sent to his sponsor in London."},{"id":"hassan","name":"Reis Hassan Osman","age":58,"height":"5 ft 7 in","role":"Reis (foreman) of the workmen","bio":"Leads eighty workmen, most from his own village of Qurna. Thirty-five seasons in the Valley; he knows its rock and sand better than any foreigner.","interest":"Yesterday morning Sir Roderick accused his men of stealing a gold bead and threatened to send all eighty home. Hassan found the body."}],"rooms":{"hill":"<b>The hillside.</b> Rock under loose <b>yellow</b> drift sand, blown in off the desert. It is the only yellow sand here: the valley floor, the paths and the whole of the tomb are covered in white limestone chip and dust from the digging.","rock":"<b>Hyena's Rock.</b> A great boulder and slabs on the hillside, a ten-minute climb up the path from the camp. Sir Roderick often went up to smoke his pipe there at night. It stands directly above the Seventh Chamber, forty feet overhead.","stairs":"<b>The tomb steps.</b> Sixteen steps cut down into the rock from the valley floor to the gate. The sand at the foot is swept smooth every evening at lock-up.","post":"<b>Tomb guard's post.</b> Suleiman Abdallah sits here by his brazier from sunset to sunrise, at the top of the steps, looking straight down them to the gate.","vane":"<b>Sir Roderick's tent.</b> Camp bed (not slept in), desk, diary, and under the bed a steel <b>strongbox</b> with four combination dials. Nobody else knew the combination.","coyle":"<b>Dr Coyle's tent.</b> Camp bed, trunk, and a desk against the back wall with a lamp. The guard's round passes in front of it.","darkroom":"<b>The darkroom.</b> A double-walled tent lit only by a red lamp, with tanks for developing and washing glass plates. It stands at the foot of the hill path.","evelyn":"<b>Miss Marsh's tent.</b> Camp bed, cameras in their cases, boxes of glass plates.","mess":"<b>The mess tent.</b> Everyone dined here from seven until half past eight last night, Sir Roderick included.","water":"<b>The water store.</b> A row of big clay water jars (<i>zirs</i>), filled from donkey-skins brought up from the Nile. Khalil, the water-boy, fills each tent's jar and lamp by a rota.","rest":"<b>The Antiquities rest house.</b> A little stone house where Dr Hanafi lives and works. The Service's key to the tomb gate is kept here in his locked despatch case.","huts":"<b>The workmen's huts.</b> Reis Hassan and thirty of the men sleep here. The rest walk home to Qurna each night.","gate":"<b>The gate.</b> An iron grille across the tomb entrance, padlocked. There are two keys: Sir Roderick's, and the Antiquities Service's.","corr":"<b>The corridors.</b> Cut through the rock and cleared by the workmen. White limestone dust underfoot.","c1":"<b>Chamber I.</b> Empty, under a painted ceiling of stars.","c2":"<b>Chamber II, the pillared hall.</b> Four square pillars painted with the treasurer and his wife. Cleared last season.","c3":"<b>Chamber III.</b> Where the treasurer's statue stands. Dr Coyle made a life-size plaster cast of its head and shoulders in November.","c4":"<b>Chamber IV.</b> A store room, cleared last season.","c5":"<b>Chamber V.</b> Empty. Robbed in ancient times, like most tombs in the Valley.","c6":"<b>Chamber VI.</b> The ante-room to the sealed doorway. The workmen's baskets and tools are kept here.","door7":"<b>Doorway VII.</b> Blocked with stones and plastered over in ancient times, stamped all over with the seals of the royal necropolis, and painted with a docket listing what lies behind it. The seals were unbroken until yesterday's breach.","c7":"<b>The Seventh Chamber.</b> Where Sir Roderick was found. Painted walls, wooden chests, jars, and rows of little servant figures."},"map":"\n<svg class=\"map\" id=\"tombmap\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 1000\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Plan of the camp above and Tomb 71 below\">\n  <style>#tombmap .lbl{font-size:22px} #tombmap .lbl-s{font-size:17px} #tombmap .xdoor{font-size:15px}</style>\n  <defs>\n    <pattern id=\"grasspat\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\"><rect width=\"14\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#f1e2b0\"/><circle cx=\"3\" cy=\"4\" r=\"1.1\" fill=\"#c9ad63\"/><circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"1.1\" fill=\"#c9ad63\"/><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"3\" r=\".8\" fill=\"#d8bf7a\"/></pattern>\n    <pattern id=\"chippat\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#f8f5ec\"/><path d=\"M4 5 l3 1 M12 13 l3 -1\" stroke=\"#d6cfbd\"/></pattern>\n    <pattern id=\"rockpat\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" patternTransform=\"rotate(45)\"><rect width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#e9e0cb\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"10\" stroke=\"#d6cbb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></pattern>\n  </defs>\n\n  <!-- ABOVE GROUND -->\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"980\" height=\"500\" fill=\"url(#chippat)\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <path class=\"rm grass\" data-room=\"hill\" d=\"M10 10 H990 V285 C 930 270, 870 240, 800 215 C 700 185, 580 165, 460 158 C 340 152, 200 150, 10 140 Z\" style=\"stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M10 148 C 200 158, 340 160, 460 166 C 580 173, 700 193, 800 223 C 870 248, 930 278, 990 293\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 6\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"420\" y=\"70\">THE HILLSIDE · loose yellow drift sand over rock</text>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"420\" y=\"92\">the camp, the paths and the tomb are all white limestone chip</text>\n  <path d=\"M725 305 C 735 262, 760 230, 790 200 C 815 176, 830 156, 838 136\" stroke=\"#c7ab6c\" stroke-width=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"742\" y=\"190\" transform=\"rotate(-48 742 190)\">hill path</text>\n  <path class=\"rm\" data-room=\"rock\" d=\"M800 92 C 808 66, 858 58, 880 76 C 898 92, 892 122, 866 130 C 840 138, 806 128, 800 110 Z\"/>\n  <path d=\"M818 84 l22 18 M852 74 l-8 40 M868 92 l14 10\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"905\" y=\"160\">Hyena's Rock</text>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"905\" y=\"178\">above Chamber VII</text>\n\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"stairs\" x=\"150\" y=\"150\" width=\"70\" height=\"48\"/>\n  <path d=\"M156 158 h58 M156 166 h58 M156 174 h58 M156 182 h58 M156 190 h58\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"185\" y=\"222\">Tomb 71</text><text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"185\" y=\"240\">steps down</text>\n  <circle class=\"rm\" data-room=\"post\" cx=\"258\" cy=\"190\" r=\"13\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"278\" y=\"196\" style=\"text-anchor:start\">tomb guard</text>\n\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"rest\" x=\"36\" y=\"286\" width=\"176\" height=\"100\" style=\"stroke-width:5\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"124\" y=\"330\">Rest house</text><text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"124\" y=\"352\">Antiquities Service</text><text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"124\" y=\"370\">Dr Hanafi</text>\n  <path d=\"M60 390 C 70 430, 60 470, 30 500\" stroke=\"#c7ab6c\" stroke-width=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"110\" y=\"485\">track to the Nile &amp; Luxor</text>\n\n  <path d=\"M285 232 H735 V462 H285 Z M285 342 H735\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8a7a5a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 6\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"560\" y=\"356\">camp guard's round</text>\n  \n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"vane\" x=\"320\" y=\"250\" width=\"120\" height=\"64\" rx=\"4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"326\" y1=\"282\" x2=\"434\" y2=\"282\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"380\" y=\"304\">Sir Roderick</text>\n  \n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"coyle\" x=\"470\" y=\"250\" width=\"110\" height=\"64\" rx=\"4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"476\" y1=\"282\" x2=\"574\" y2=\"282\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"525\" y=\"304\">Dr Coyle</text>\n  <rect x=\"505\" y=\"253\" width=\"40\" height=\"8\" fill=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"525\" cy=\"268\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--brass)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"darkroom\" x=\"610\" y=\"258\" width=\"100\" height=\"58\" rx=\"4\" style=\"stroke-width:4\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"660\" y=\"292\">Darkroom</text>\n  \n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"mess\" x=\"300\" y=\"372\" width=\"160\" height=\"72\" rx=\"4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"306\" y1=\"408\" x2=\"454\" y2=\"408\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"380\" y=\"434\">Mess tent</text>\n  <rect x=\"340\" y=\"384\" width=\"80\" height=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"water\" x=\"490\" y=\"380\" width=\"90\" height=\"54\" rx=\"4\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"508\" cy=\"420\" r=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"528\" cy=\"420\" r=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"548\" cy=\"420\" r=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"566\" cy=\"420\" r=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"535\" y=\"400\">water store</text>\n  \n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"evelyn\" x=\"610\" y=\"372\" width=\"110\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"616\" y1=\"402\" x2=\"714\" y2=\"402\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"665\" y=\"422\">Miss Marsh</text>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"huts\" x=\"770\" y=\"330\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\"/>\n  <path d=\"M790 350 h40 v30 h-40z M850 350 h40 v30 h-40z M910 350 h40 v30 h-40z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"870\" y=\"420\">Workmen's huts</text><text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"870\" y=\"442\">Reis Hassan and 30 men</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(60 70)\"><path d=\"M0 -26 L9 7 L0 0 L-9 7Z\" fill=\"var(--ink)\"/><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"0\" y=\"-32\">N</text></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(300 492)\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"55\" y=\"-8\" >100 yards</text></g>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"870\" y=\"500\" style=\"text-anchor:middle\">ABOVE GROUND · THE CAMP</text>\n\n  <!-- BELOW GROUND -->\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"530\" width=\"980\" height=\"460\" fill=\"url(#rockpat)\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"30\" y=\"566\" style=\"text-anchor:start\">BELOW GROUND · TOMB 71</text>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"30\" y=\"588\" style=\"text-anchor:start\">plan · solid rock all round</text>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"840\" y=\"662\">↑ Hyena's Rock is 40 ft overhead</text>\n\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"stairs\" x=\"40\" y=\"750\" width=\"110\" height=\"40\"/>\n  <path d=\"M48 752 v36 M55 752 v36 M62 752 v36 M69 752 v36 M76 752 v36 M83 752 v36 M90 752 v36 M97 752 v36 M104 752 v36 M111 752 v36 M118 752 v36 M125 752 v36 M132 752 v36 M139 752 v36 M146 752 v36\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"95\" y=\"740\">16 steps down</text>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"gate\" x=\"150\" y=\"744\" width=\"14\" height=\"52\"/>\n  <path d=\"M157 746 v48\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"3\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"xdoor\" x=\"157\" y=\"812\">GATE</text>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"corr\" x=\"164\" y=\"755\" width=\"136\" height=\"30\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"232\" y=\"775\">corridor</text>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"c1\" x=\"300\" y=\"720\" width=\"90\" height=\"100\"/><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"345\" y=\"776\">I</text>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"corr\" x=\"390\" y=\"755\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\"/>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"c2\" x=\"420\" y=\"680\" width=\"150\" height=\"180\"/>\n  <g fill=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"><rect x=\"452\" y=\"716\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"/><rect x=\"522\" y=\"716\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"/><rect x=\"452\" y=\"808\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"/><rect x=\"522\" y=\"808\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"/></g>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"495\" y=\"770\">II</text><text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"495\" y=\"790\">pillared hall</text>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"c3\" x=\"465\" y=\"600\" width=\"60\" height=\"80\"/><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"495\" y=\"646\">III</text>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"c4\" x=\"465\" y=\"860\" width=\"60\" height=\"80\"/><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"495\" y=\"906\">IV</text>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"corr\" x=\"570\" y=\"755\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\"/>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"c5\" x=\"600\" y=\"720\" width=\"80\" height=\"100\"/><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"640\" y=\"776\">V</text>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"corr\" x=\"680\" y=\"755\" width=\"20\" height=\"30\"/>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"c6\" x=\"700\" y=\"715\" width=\"70\" height=\"110\"/><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"735\" y=\"776\">VI</text>\n  <line class=\"door\" x1=\"300\" y1=\"758\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"782\"/><line class=\"door\" x1=\"390\" y1=\"758\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"782\"/>\n  <line class=\"door\" x1=\"420\" y1=\"758\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"782\"/><line class=\"door\" x1=\"570\" y1=\"758\" x2=\"570\" y2=\"782\"/>\n  <line class=\"door\" x1=\"600\" y1=\"758\" x2=\"600\" y2=\"782\"/><line class=\"door\" x1=\"680\" y1=\"758\" x2=\"680\" y2=\"782\"/>\n  <line class=\"door\" x1=\"700\" y1=\"758\" x2=\"700\" y2=\"782\"/><line class=\"door\" x1=\"164\" y1=\"758\" x2=\"164\" y2=\"782\"/>\n  <line class=\"door\" x1=\"483\" y1=\"680\" x2=\"507\" y2=\"680\"/><line class=\"door\" x1=\"483\" y1=\"860\" x2=\"507\" y2=\"860\"/>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"door7\" x=\"770\" y=\"742\" width=\"14\" height=\"56\" style=\"fill:#cdbd9b\"/>\n  <line x1=\"777\" y1=\"798\" x2=\"745\" y2=\"838\" stroke=\"var(--red)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><text class=\"xdoor\" x=\"720\" y=\"856\">DOORWAY VII</text>\n  <rect class=\"rm\" data-room=\"c7\" x=\"784\" y=\"680\" width=\"150\" height=\"180\"/>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\">\n    <rect x=\"794\" y=\"690\" width=\"34\" height=\"22\"/><rect x=\"794\" y=\"720\" width=\"34\" height=\"22\"/><rect x=\"886\" y=\"826\" width=\"36\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"842\" y=\"826\" width=\"36\" height=\"24\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"800\" cy=\"818\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"800\" cy=\"840\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"816\" cy=\"840\" r=\"6\"/>\n    <path d=\"M846 698 h30 M846 706 h30 M846 714 h30\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 3\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M902 682 C 912 690, 930 688, 932 684 L 932 724 C 918 724, 904 712, 902 700 Z\" fill=\"url(#grasspat)\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"905\" y=\"672\" style=\"font-size:14px\">heap of rock &amp; sand</text>\n  <rect x=\"872\" y=\"770\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--red)\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" pointer-events=\"none\"/>\n  <text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"895\" y=\"804\" style=\"fill:var(--red)\">body</text>\n  <text class=\"lbl\" x=\"830\" y=\"786\">VII</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(60 650)\"><path d=\"M0 -26 L9 7 L0 0 L-9 7Z\" fill=\"var(--ink)\"/><text class=\"lbl\" x=\"0\" y=\"-32\">N</text></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(820 968)\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text class=\"lbl-s\" x=\"50\" y=\"-8\">50 feet</text></g>\n  <g id=\"tracks\"></g>\n</svg>","evidence":[{"id":"x-scene","kind":"report","title":"The Seventh Chamber","sub":"Inspector Fawzi, 7.30 a.m.","html":"\n      <figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"img/d-tomb/chamber.jpg\" alt=\"The Seventh Chamber by lamplight\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Inside the Seventh Chamber, looking back towards the widened doorway and Chamber VI.</figcaption></figure>\n      <ol class=\"inv\">\n        <li><b>Body</b> face down at the back of the chamber, twenty feet from the doorway.</li>\n        <li><b>Wound:</b> one heavy blow to the back of the head. Beside him, a round <b>dolerite pounder</b>, a stone the ancient masons used. Several lie about the floor.</li>\n        <li><b>His hurricane lamp</b> on its side, out, the glass cracked.</li>\n        <li><b>Clothes:</b> the knees and elbows of his suit and the whole front of his coat are thick with <b>fine yellow sand</b>. There is yellow sand in his hair and in his trouser turn-ups.</li>\n        <li><b>Pockets:</b> pipe, tobacco, matches, a pencil. His gate key is on his watch chain.</li>\n        <li><b>The chamber:</b> chests, jars and rows of little figures along the walls. In the far corner, a heap of fallen rock and yellow sand, which Dr Coyle says came down from the ceiling in ancient times.</li>\n      </ol>"},{"id":"x-doors","kind":"report","title":"The doorway and the gate","sub":"Inspector Fawzi, with Reis Hassan","html":"\n      <p><b>Doorway VII.</b> Reis Hassan's men broke the hole at 3.30 yesterday afternoon, with Sir Roderick and Dr Hanafi watching. It is at the top of the doorway, five feet off the floor, and measures <b>11 inches by 14 inches</b>. This morning it was exactly as they left it: sharp plaster edges, not a scrape, the rubble beneath it undisturbed. Every seal round it is whole.</p>\n      <p>Sir Roderick stood 6 ft 1 and weighed seventeen stone. He could not have got more than his head and one arm through. At 7.10 a.m. we widened the hole to reach him.</p>\n      <p><b>The gate.</b> Sir Roderick locked it himself at 5.15 p.m. At lock-up the guard swept the sand at the foot of the steps smooth, as he does every night. At 6.15 this morning the padlock was fast and the sand smooth. The only marks in it were made by Dr Hanafi and Reis Hassan as they opened up.</p>"},{"id":"x-suleiman","kind":"statement","who":"Suleiman Abdallah, tomb guard","title":"Statement: the tomb guard","sub":"Suleiman Abdallah, taken 7.45 a.m.","html":"\n      <p>\"From sunset until the reis came at six, I sat at the top of the steps by my fire. Nobody went down those steps and nobody came up. I would have seen a mouse.</p>\n      <p>At ten minutes past eleven, by my watch, I heard a shout from deep under the ground. One shout, a man's voice, far away, and then nothing. I called down through the grille and nobody answered. The gate was locked and the sand was smooth, so I told myself it was a jackal on the hill. I am sorry now that I did.\"</p>"},{"id":"x-abdelaal","kind":"statement","who":"Abdel-Aal Mahmoud, camp guard","title":"Statement: the camp guard","sub":"Abdel-Aal Mahmoud, taken 8.00 a.m.","html":"\n      <figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"img/d-tomb/tent.jpg\" alt=\"A tent lit from inside at night\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A lamp-lit tent in the camp at night, from the guard's path.</figcaption></figure>\n      <p>\"I walk the round of the tents from sunset until midnight, once every half hour. Then Ibrahim takes over.</p>\n      <p>At twenty to eleven Sir Roderick came out of his tent with his lamp lit and went up the path behind the darkroom, towards Hyena's Rock. I watched his lamp climb the hill until it went in among the rocks.</p>\n      <p>Dr Coyle's lamp burned in his tent all night. Each time I passed, at half past ten, eleven, half past eleven and midnight, I saw his shadow on the canvas, bent over his desk. He did not stir. A hard worker, the Doctor.</p>\n      <p>At eleven, and again at half past, Miss Marsh put her head out of the darkroom and asked me for a can of water. I handed it to her myself. The rest house was dark from ten, and the reis was in the huts with the men.\"</p>"},{"id":"x-hassan","kind":"statement","who":"hassan","title":"Statement: Reis Hassan Osman","sub":"Taken 8.15 a.m.","html":"\n      <p>\"At six Sir Roderick was not in his tent and his bed had not been slept in. Dr Hanafi opened the gate with his key, and I held my lamp to the hole in the Seventh doorway. He was lying at the back.</p>\n      <p>The sand up on the hill is yellow, from the desert; down here everything is white from our digging. Last season I took Sir Roderick a photograph of Hyena's Rock and asked to clear it. He tore it up in front of me. I kept the pieces.</p>\n      <p>Yesterday he said my men had stolen a gold bead, and he would send them all home. He could not say where from. My men are not thieves.\"</p>"},{"id":"p-rock","kind":"puzzle","type":"jigsaw","title":"The torn photograph","sub":"Nine pieces, kept by Reis Hassan","html":"\n      <p>A print of Hyena's Rock, torn into nine by Sir Roderick last season. There is writing on the back.</p>","data":{"img":"img/d-tomb/rock.jpg"},"after":"<p>Hyena's Rock and the drift sand, looking down towards the valley. On the back, in the reis's pencil (Dr Hanafi translates the Arabic):</p>\n      <p class=\"hand\">Hyena's Rock stands straight over the Seventh Chamber. The old robbers liked to dig down into a tomb from above. Let us clear the Rock before the chamber is opened.</p>\n      <p>Under it, in Sir Roderick's hand: <span class=\"hand-inline\">No. Leave the Rock alone. R.V.</span></p>"},{"id":"x-coyle","kind":"statement","who":"coyle","title":"Statement: Dr Leonard Coyle","sub":"Taken 8.30 a.m.","html":"\n      <p>\"After dinner I went to my tent to write up the docket on the doorway for the newspapermen. I was at my desk until well after midnight. The guard saw me every time he went by.</p>\n      <p>That hole in the doorway? A cat could hardly get through it. How Roderick got in there I cannot begin to think. You might ask who else holds a key to that gate.\"</p>"},{"id":"x-evelyn","kind":"statement","who":"evelyn","title":"Statement: Miss Evelyn Marsh","sub":"Taken 8.45 a.m.","html":"\n      <p>\"I was in the darkroom from half past nine until about one, developing yesterday's plates of the breach. I heard Sir Roderick go past at about twenty to eleven, whistling, up the hill path. He often went up to the Rock to smoke.</p>\n      <p>Yes, he caught me sending prints to the <i>Courier</i>, and he said he'd finish me. I was furious. I didn't kill him for it.\"</p>"},{"id":"x-hanafi","kind":"statement","who":"hanafi","title":"Statement: Dr Yusuf Hanafi","sub":"Taken 9.00 a.m.","html":"\n      <p>\"Yesterday afternoon I copied the docket painted on the Seventh doorway. At dinner I said I would go through the chamber with it in the morning, item by item, before any newspaperman set foot inside. Sir Roderick did not like that. We quarrelled, as we have all season: he wanted half the finds for London, and the law of Egypt now says no.</p>\n      <p>The Service's key was in my despatch case, locked, all night. I put out my lamp at ten. I opened the gate at a quarter past six with the reis beside me.\"</p>"}],"question":{"kind":"final","prompt":"How did Sir Roderick get into the Seventh Chamber?","help":"Choose one.","fields":[{"id":"how","label":"Way in","options":[["gate","Down the steps and through the gate, with his key"],["breach","Through the hole broken in the sealed doorway"],["shut","He never left the tomb: he was locked in at sunset"],["hill","By a hidden way in from the hillside above"]]}],"hints":["Rule out the ways you can. Measure him against the hole, and read what the tomb guard and the sand say about the gate.","Where does yellow sand come from? Where was Sir Roderick seen going at twenty to eleven? Piece together the torn photograph and read the back."]}},"locked":{"s2":"","s3":"","sol":""}};
